
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html

Web authentication and presence regression tests (Node.js, no dependencies):

    node test/web-sessions.test.cjs
    TEST_WEB_LOCKS=1 node test/web-sessions.test.cjs

These execute the real op.js controller with separate simulated tabs and a
mock Firebase transport. They cover duplication, focus, reconnect, refresh,
revocation races, offline logout, server clock offset and validation failures.
They do not replace a browser/Firebase integration test.

Presence behavior:
- A stable sessionStorage ID owns a tab row; each connection has a separate ID.
- Web Locks (or BroadcastChannel ownership probes) separate duplicated tabs.
- Only the current connection determines Online; heartbeat expires after 20 s.
- Revoked sessions remain as hidden markers, so delayed writes cannot restore
  visible rows. Do not delete these markers while old clients may reconnect.
- Offline logout completes locally. Pending server revocations are retried by
  another authenticated same-origin tab or at the next authenticated connection.
- On deployment, already open pages must reload to use the new controller.
